    "reason": "The only evidence is the changelog line [ev-a56a8cf82a6c], \"feat(rbac)!: disable fine-grained inheritance by default\". \"By default\" means this is a default change on some setting, but the evidence doesn't name that setting (config key, flag or Helm value) or give its before/after values. Without them, neither the subject identity nor whether the change should be default-changed (with literals) rather than behavior-changed can be settled. RBAC inheritance is also not clearly wire/protocol behaviour, so the protocol-behavior family is doubtful. Deciding needs the upgrade-guide text or PR (#19988/#20671) that names the controlling key and its old and new defaults.",
